    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29151" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσ-κλεής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>inglorious</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.22
			</span></i> (poet. acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσκλέᾰ</span> for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσκλεέα</span>); <i>infamous,
				shameful</i>, of persons and things, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. θέα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					243
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσκλεεστάτῳ μόρῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					444
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρῶτον μὲν οὐκ οὖσ᾽ ἄδικός εἰμι
					δυσκλεής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					270
				</span></i>
			. cf.<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				3.3.53
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>3 Ma.</u>
				3.23
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			). Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εῶς</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				1006
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				993
			</span></i> codd., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.169a
			</span></i>.</div>
